## FILE OPERATIONS AND PERMISSIONS

**Learning Objective:** Master file manipulation and the Linux permission model (read/write/execute, `chmod`, `chown`).

---

## File Operation Commands

| Command | What it does | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `cp` | Copy a file or directory | `cp app.js backup.js` |
| `mv` | Move or rename a file | `mv old.txt new.txt` |
| `rm` | Remove (delete) a file | `rm file.txt`, `rm -r folder/` |
| `cat` | Print a file's full contents | `cat README.md` |
| `less` | View a file page-by-page | `less app.log` (press `q` to quit) |
| `head` | Show the first lines of a file (default: 10) | `head -n 5 file.txt` |
| `tail` | Show the last lines of a file | `tail -n 20 server.log` |

**Note:** `cp` creates a new inode with its own copy of the data. `mv` doesn't touch the data at all — it's usually just a directory-entry
update, unless moving across filesystems (in which case it copies then deletes).

