## Permissions Cheat-Sheet (Deliverable)

Three files, each with a different permission combination:

```bash
touch file1.txt file2.txt file3.txt
chmod 644 file1.txt   # owner: rw-, group: r--, other: r--
chmod 600 file2.txt   # owner: rw-, group: ---, other: ---
chmod 755 file3.txt   # owner: rwx, group: r-x, other: r-x
ls -l
```

| File | Permissions | Who can do what |
|---|---|---|
| `file1.txt` | `644` | Owner can read/write. Group and others can only read. |
| `file2.txt` | `600` | Owner can read/write. No one else has any access. |
| `file3.txt` | `755` | Owner can read/write/execute. Group and others can read/execute, not write. |
